FEATURE: example-redesign
DATE: 2026-08-26
SCOPE: bring the three older example pages up to the design standard, on a shared system
FOLLOWS: changelog/changelog-requirement

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AFFECTED PROJECTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

vUX library (this repository) — examples and conventions only. No library source changed.

  - examples/shared/example.css   new — tokens and primitives for all example pages
  - examples/modal/               redesigned; five sections, live config, error demos
  - examples/form/                redesigned; widget palette driven from page tokens
  - examples/spa/                 redesigned; sticky nav, styled route content, /shared/ mapping
  - examples/autowriter/          retrofitted onto the shared stylesheet
  - CLAUDE.md                     documents the shared stylesheet; stale note retired

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Feature 'example-design-standard' set a standard that only one of the four example pages
met, and recorded the other three as out of step. This closes that gap.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT CHANGED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

A shared design system was extracted first, so the four pages share one palette and one
set of primitives instead of four diverging copies. Each page then keeps only what is
specific to its own demo.

Every demonstration the three pages already made is preserved. What was added is what the
standard names and they lacked: a hero that leads with the component working, live
controls for config properties that had been fixed in code, and a section that performs
bad calls and prints what was thrown.

Each page also had one structural problem the redesign had to solve, and each is now
documented rather than left to be rediscovered:

  - modal — content is moved into an overlay outside the page wrapper, so it is styled
    standalone; and #page must not wrap it, or the blur mode blurs the dialog too.
  - form — the component generates the widgets' stylesheets from config strings, so
    re-theming means re-theming those strings. main.js now interpolates one palette
    object into them, so widget colours and page CSS cannot drift apart.
  - spa — route fragments are injected at runtime and carry no classes, so they are
    styled through the boundary element and stay portable content.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PUBLIC API
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Unchanged. No library file was touched.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NOT DONE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  - The pages were not opened in a browser — there is none in this environment — so
    every visual result across all four is unconfirmed. Everything verifiable without
    rendering was verified.
  - src/helpers.js validateInteger() still returns a boolean instead of throwing.
    Outstanding since 'auto-writer-fixes'.
  - Nine modules still have neither a guide nor an example: Carousel, FormValidator,
    ListScroller, TouchHandler, ToolTip, Resizer, TimeLineList, CShapes, DOMDrawer.
    They are now the only thing standing between the library and full coverage.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
VERIFICATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Every error demo on all three pages was checked against the real validators from
src/helpers.js using the exact values each button passes — 14 for modal, 15 for form
(including the values the pages themselves use, to confirm the live configuration is
valid), 5 for spa. All passing.

Selectors were cross-checked between each main.js and its markup. Both servers were run:
the static server for modal/form/autowriter, and the SPA dev server, where every URL the
page needs returned 200 including the new /shared/ mapping and the two client-side routes
through the history fallback. The AutoWriter suites (29 module + 30 example assertions)
were re-run unchanged after the stylesheet extraction. server.py re-checked for syntax.
